{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q138004200","formula":"C₁₀H₁₂INO₃","hill":"C10H12INO3","elements":["H","C","N","O","I"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":12.0,"I":1.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Βk-2C-I"},"descriptions":{"en":"βk-2C-I, or bk-2C-I, also known as β-keto-4-iodo-2,5-dimethoxyphenethylamine or as β-keto-2C-I, is a psychedelic drug of the phenethylamine and 2C families related to 2C-I. It is the β-keto derivative of 2C-I and is cathinone-like in chemical structure. The drug is closely related to βk-2C-B. It is said to have a longer duration than 2C-I and to not be as intense in its effects as βk-2C-B. Concerns have been expressed about the potential toxicity of the iodine in βk-2C-I. The interactions of βk-2C-I with monoamine oxidase have been studied. βk-2C-I was encountered as a novel designer drug online by at least 2016 and was first described in the scientific literature by 2018."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":165361441,"mass":321.11,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=CC(=C(C=C1C(=O)CN)OC)I","inchikey":"SGQREGRMRKZYSF-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-amino-1-(4-iodo-2,5-dimethoxyphenyl)ethanone","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"165361441","atoms":27,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.144,"y":-2.489,"z":-0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.661,"y":-1.428,"z":0.798,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.404,"y":-0.997,"z":0.469,"el":"C"},{"x":0.644,"y":-1.906,"z":0.283,"el":"C"},{"x":1.944,"y":-1.448,"z":0.035,"el":"C"},{"x":2.227,"y":-0.076,"z":-0.008,"el":"C"},{"x":1.179,"y":0.826,"z":0.195,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.136,"y":0.376,"z":0.427,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.174,"y":1.433,"z":0.616,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.841,"y":2.494,"z":1.15,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.594,"y":1.227,"z":0.105,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.598,"y":0.947,"z":-1.338,"el":"N"},{"x":3.524,"y":0.292,"z":-0.25,"el":"O"},{"x":3.844,"y":1.676,"z":-